        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6,
          "end": 9.66,
          "en": "Now, Hibernate is an ORM framework,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.66,
          "end": 12.66,
          "en": "but the question is what is ORM?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.66,
          "end": 16.29,
          "en": "ORM stands for Object Relational Mapping.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.29,
          "end": 17.88,
          "en": "The next question is why do we need it?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.88,
          "end": 19.56,
          "en": "See, the thing is when we talk about Java,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.56,
          "end": 22.08,
          "en": "and we have talked about it, Java is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 22.08,
          "end": 23.16,
          "en": "oriented language.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.16,
          "end": 25.83,
          "en": "Everything in that is object, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 25.83,
          "end": 27.78,
          "en": "And when you build an application with Java,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 29.37,
          "en": "the first thing which comes to your mind is object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 29.37,
          "end": 31.92,
          "en": "Whatever you wanna do, it should be an object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 31.92,
          "end": 35.7,
          "en": "Let's say if you want to build a application, every entity",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 38.85,
          "en": "that if you want to represent a person or a thing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 38.85,
          "end": 42.54,
          "en": "or any operation, you first think about object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 42.54,
          "end": 44.73,
          "en": "And then we think about, okay, with this object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 44.73,
          "end": 46.62,
          "en": "what operations I can perform.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 46.62,
          "end": 49.71,
          "en": "So every object will have data and methods.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.71,
          "end": 51.51,
          "en": "Now, if you want to store this data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 51.51,
          "end": 52.35,
          "en": "how will you store that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 52.35,
          "end": 54.69,
          "en": "Of course, we want a permanent storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 54.69,
          "end": 56.82,
          "en": "not in a memory.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 56.82,
          "end": 58.23,
          "en": "Now when you talk about permanent storage,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 58.23,
          "end": 60.18,
          "en": "of course you can save this data in a file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 60.18,
          "end": 62.55,
          "en": "You can store this data in, I mean when I say file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 62.55,
          "end": 65.88,
          "en": "it can be CSU file or any other type of file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 65.88,
          "end": 67.38,
          "en": "But if you want to store that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 67.38,
          "end": 68.73,
          "en": "so that you can also process it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 68.73,
          "end": 71.67,
          "en": "that's where we want some good type of databases.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 71.67,
          "end": 74.22,
          "en": "Now of course, this can be a relational one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 74.22,
          "end": 76.23,
          "en": "or this can be a non-relational one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 76.23,
          "end": 79.32,
          "en": "which you also call NoSQL databases.",
