        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 245.58,
          "end": 249.33,
          "en": "If your columns, we have three fields there in the class.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 249.33,
          "end": 252.51,
          "en": "Can we create three columns here? What about the names?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 252.51,
          "end": 255.18,
          "en": "Same names, it's just that in there, in Java",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 255.18,
          "end": 256.41,
          "en": "we use camel casing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 256.41,
          "end": 258.12,
          "en": "Here we'll be using sneak casing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 258.12,
          "end": 259.44,
          "en": "What about the type?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 259.44,
          "end": 261.6,
          "en": "The same type, whatever you have in Java,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 261.6,
          "end": 263.04,
          "en": "we'll try to match it with a table.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 263.04,
          "end": 266.07,
          "en": "So let's say if it's int, int, then string text.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 266.07,
          "end": 268.32,
          "en": "That's how we can match it. And what about the data?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 268.32,
          "end": 269.91,
          "en": "Every object have different data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 269.91,
          "end": 272.43,
          "en": "So each object becomes one row.",
